course: dictionary
lesson: 1808
title: Cloven: split in two
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Cloven» means split into two parts. Look at the clues around it. The sentence talks about walking on two toes, so a cloven hoof is a hoof split into two toes.
explain: «Cows, sheep, goats and pigs walk on two toes, called cloven hooves, with two smaller dewclaws higher up at the back.» A horse, on the other hand, walks on one toe on each foot. Try your meaning in the sentence: «two toes, called split hooves» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Cloven is an old form of the verb cleave, which means to split. Old writers also used cloven to mean split apart by a strong blow. In these older books, the word may look strange, but the idea of splitting is always there.
fact: «Cloven» means split into two parts.
fact: Cows, sheep, goats, pigs and deer have cloven hooves, with two toes on each foot.
fact: A horse has a single solid hoof, so it is not cloven.
fact: In old stories, the Devil is often drawn with cloven hooves, so «showing the cloven hoof» meant showing a wicked side.
fact: In old writing, «cloven» can also mean split or cut apart by a strong blow.
exercise: «Cows, sheep, goats and pigs walk on two toes, called cloven hooves.» What does cloven mean? | Shiny and smooth | *Split into two parts | Very old | Solid and in one piece
exercise: «A horse walks on one solid toe on each foot.» Does a horse have cloven hooves? | Yes, it is split into two toes | Yes, it has many small toes | No, it has no hooves at all | *No, it has one solid hoof
exercise: Which animal has cloven hooves? | Snake | *Pig | Dog | Horse
test: In old stories, «showing the cloven hoof» means showing what? | A hungry mood | A long journey | A kind side | *A wicked side
test: In old writing, «cloven» can mean split apart by a strong blow. Which word means the same here? | *Split | Soft | Sleepy | Whole
exam: Read this: «Cows, sheep, goats and pigs walk on two toes, called cloven hooves, with two smaller dewclaws higher up at the back.» Which word tells you the hooves are split? | *Cloven | Walk | Higher | Dewclaws
